cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Reproducible Documents: A hands-on tutorial for Stata users
message: >-
  If you use these materials, please cite them as below.
type: presentation
authors:
  - given-names: Lars
    family-names: Vilhuber
    email: lars.vilhuber@cornell.edu
    affiliation: Cornell University
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5733-8932'
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/larsvilhuber/reproducible-documents/
abstract: >-
  Numbers typed by hand into a paper drift out of date, and cannot be traced
  to the code that produced them. This tutorial walks researchers who know
  Stata through four ways to create documents in which every number comes
  from the code: Quarto on posit.cloud, Stata-generated LaTeX macros, Stata's
  dyndoc with Word output, and Jupyter notebooks running Stata on Google Colab.
